iven macroeconomic volatility.    - Use technical indicators (e.g., moving averages, RSI) to confirm entry points, favoring when momentum is positive.    - Monitor supply chain developments and global economic signals closely, ready to adjust exposure if macro risks escalate.    - Consider scaling into related positions in Apple’s suppliers or complementary tech companies aligned with Apple’s strategic moves.  In reflecting on past mistakes where I overly relied on optimistic narratives without sufficient risk appraisal, I will now incorporate a balanced view—acknowledging growth opportunities while vigilantly managing downside risks. This disciplined approach should improve future decision-making and protect against unforeseen adverse developments.
